  "answer_markdown": "In Search Toolkit 0.0.9, after switching to the deterministic document identity model, the following changes occur regarding the `id` fields on `File` and `DocumentChunk`:\n\n1. **Explicit `id` field on `File`**: This field has been **removed** to enforce deterministic identity generation based on `source_id` and `locator` instead of random values [1].\n\n2. **`document_id` field on `DocumentChunk`**: This field has also been **removed**, as chunk IDs are now computed deterministically from the combination of `source_id` and `locator` [1].\n\n### How IDs are computed now:\n- **`Document.id`**: A UUID5 hash derived from the `source_id` [2].\n- **`DocumentChunk.id`**: A UUID5 hash derived from the combination of `source_id` + `locator` [2].\n- **`parent_ref`**: A hash of the `source_id`, ensuring chunks always resolve back to their parent document [2].\n\nThis deterministic approach ensures that re-ingesting the same `source_id` and locators will overwrite existing records instead of creating duplicates, making indexing **idempotent** [2].",

